{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: recover the undelivered Stage B of conservative Tailapp-source upgrades from #2273/#2764. Queue after the existing full I7, Kiro4055, install4129, guard4131, URL4087 and analytics4161 commitments; keep those outcomes intact. Answer with your availability and the retained full outcome, or a concrete viability issue.\n\nThe [Stage B audit](conservative-upgrades-audit.json) shows #2764 commissioned design followed by implementation, but promise1804bbc3 covered only the design. Approval4f99068a and receipt240ed43a landed exactly one note at c35789d6; they did not deliver its four implementation stages. Current main3a593 contains that note unchanged, and the [CLI dispatch](internal/cli/cli.go@3a593721231326d589541113add606b270490e35:309) has no upgrade-plan or upgrade command. Actual go-run probes in an empty temporary home return unknown apps subcommand for both, while apps help succeeds and no home files are created. No later Stage B assignment or explicit abandonment was found through frontier4175. The completed binary-upgrade and runtime-guidance work must remain complete.\n\nRetain the full outcome in the [accepted Stage A design](notes/2026-08-31-conservative-tailapp-upgrades.md@3a593721231326d589541113add606b270490e35:162): (1) durable first-party provenance, signed release metadata and read-only classification/three-way plan; (2) certified pristine-built-in apply-safe through optimistic validation and continuation, with failure/race protection; (3) explicit app-selected continue/reset with acknowledgement, user-selected coherent backup and verified restore; (4) CLI/MCP/schema/docs/integration delivery against runtime upgrade-pending behavior. A note, feasibility result, one stage or binary-only upgrade is not completion of this request.\n\nBefore implementation, reconcile the design against then-current code and I7 runtime/activation contracts, and publish a current decision proposal for Hugh's ordinary adoption. Preserve Checker advisories A1-A4: name the baseline-adoption command and stable JSON result; authenticate the release manifest under signed release checksums/attestation and define continue_safe_from as exact baseline source digests; make stopped-service/KeepAlive restore behavior explicit; keep the plan stable for MCP. Reconcile the current [registry](internal/definition/registry.go@3a593721231326d589541113add606b270490e35:88) and #4129's proven install failure semantics: registry creation and activation are not currently one atomic rollback. The new provenance/apply design must specify honest transactional and crash-recovery guarantees and test them, without rewriting the existing install contract by assertion. Ordinary adoption must precede implementation of any changed decision; an approved historical design is not proof that current authority or runtime details are unchanged.\n\nPreserve these conditions throughout: legacy/unproven installations and user-generated apps are never guessed to be built-in; modified built-ins receive a bounded baseline/current/upstream comparison and are never automatically overwritten, merged, activated or reset; certification is not inferred from schema shape, compilation or a successful test. apply-safe may touch only a pristine built-in whose exact baseline and target digests are certified for continue. Unknown, missing, malformed, untrusted or incompatible metadata refuses without fallback to reset. Explicit non-certified or reset changes require an app selection, the appropriate acknowledgement and a successful operator-selected backup before mutation. Preserve drafts and expected revisions; backup and restore must be coherent across registry, inbox and projections, bounded, integrity-checked and failure-safe. Normal binary upgrades still leave app sources, drafts, projections and telemetry settings alone.\n\nKeep the four independent stage-review checkpoints from the design. Prefer one final implementation landing after all four outcomes a